//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 89 - SUPERTREND FLIP CONTINUATION LONG. A GENUINELY NEW MECHANISM, BARE.
//
// THE STORED SCHEDULED PROMPT describes a board state ("Attack 37, build its filter stack") more than
// eighty attacks stale, instructing "continue numbering after 37." THE DOCS OVERRIDE IT, per the
// prompt's own instruction: Attack 41 closed Attack 37 on cost; the OBV-divergence filter stack on
// Attack 68/82/83 is CLOSED at three terms after Attack 71/87/88 each failed a distinct term-4
// candidate; Attack 83's own queue (item 2) named the next step as ONE genuinely new mechanism, listing
// untried indicators on this engine's 65-function allowlist including ta.supertrend, never used in any
// prior attack. This cycle builds that.
//
// ==================== WHAT THIS CLAIMS, IN ONE SENTENCE ====================
// When price closes back above the SuperTrend band (an ATR-adaptive stop-and-reverse line) after having
// been below it, the market has already absorbed enough of the prevailing volatility to flip the
// dominant trend state, and the new uptrend leg tends to continue toward a measured-move projection of
// the swing that preceded the flip before mean-reverting.
//
// ==================== WHY THIS IS A NEW INPUT CLASS FOR THIS LAB ====================
// Every prior mechanism used one of: rolling extremes with no structure filter (33, 48), a calendar
// anchor (34/35/54/55), a volatility state used as a REGIME GATE not a trigger (36, 65, 76, 78), a
// failed break of a swing low (37-43), a tap-and-reclaim of a swing level (44-47), a single bar's own
// range/volume (49), a session range (50), an RSI/price divergence (51/52), a summed order-flow-proxy
// absorption signal (53), a consecutive-close streak (56), a LAGGING EMA-slope crossover (57/58),
// confirmed price-only swing structure (59, 63), an OBV/price divergence family (66-71, 82, 83, 87, 88),
// lag-1 return autocorrelation (72), Ichimoku kumo/chikou (73), a weekend calendar window (74), a
// round-number level reclaim (75), NVI smart-money regime (76), Bollinger Band width squeeze (77),
// ADX/DMI trend-strength regime (78), MFI oversold reclaim (79), ATR/price divergence (80), and volume-
// climax capitulation (81). NONE has used an ATR-ENVELOPE STOP-AND-REVERSE LINE as the entry trigger
// itself. This is related to the EMA-slope crossover family (57/58) in that both are trend-STATE flips,
// but SuperTrend's line is not a lagging average of price -- it is a volatility-adaptive band that
// jumps discretely on a flip and is itself derived from ATR, giving it a fundamentally different
// (and typically much faster) flip timing than an EMA-slope cross. Flagged here rather than overclaimed,
// per this lab's own standard (Attack 66) of naming what a build shares with what already exists.
//
// ==================== MECHANICS, NO ARRAYS, NO USER-DEFINED FUNCTIONS ====================
// ta.supertrend(factor, atrLen) returns [st, dir], the band line and its discrete direction state.
// flipLong = ta.crossover(close, st): the bar price closes back above the band after being below it --
// a single, unambiguous, non-repainting trigger (built-in function, evaluated bar-by-bar on close,
// process_orders_on_close=true). Stop: the most recent CONFIRMED swing low (ta.pivotlow, LESSON 5,
// actual structure -- NOT the SuperTrend line itself, which is forbidden as a trailing exit under this
// lab's own fixed-SL/TP-at-entry rule and the engine's ban on custom var-trail). Target: a MEASURED-MOVE
// PROJECTION -- entry price plus the amplitude of the most recent confirmed swing (pivot high minus
// pivot low), a level derived from the swing's own geometry (HARD LESSON 41), independent of R (E14:
// minRpct constrains the stop distance; swingAmp constrains the target, drawn from a different
// quantity).
//
// AUDIT, one line per leg:
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) - enforced by EXCLUSION via rBig, never clamped.
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) - slPx = lastPivLow, the most recent confirmed swing low, not the
//        SuperTrend line and not a fixed-ATR offset from entry.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) - LONG ONLY. A bearish mirror (ta.crossunder(close, st)) is
//        untested; the short leg is a reported standing asymmetry (Attack 64).
//   BINDING (E17) - flipLong AND rBig AND swingOk all necessarily bind: flipLong alone fires on every
//        SuperTrend flip regardless of stop distance or swing validity, so rBig and swingOk each
//        independently remove flips the raw trigger would otherwise take.
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) - flipLong reads an ATR-ENVELOPE TREND-STATE (a volatility-adaptive band, a domain
//        no prior attack has used as a trigger); rBig reads PRICE DISTANCE from entry to the confirmed
//        swing low; swingOk reads PRICE SWING AMPLITUDE between the confirmed swing high and low. Three
//        independent quantities across three domains -- trend-state, stop-distance, target-geometry.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) - lastPivLow and lastPivHigh are `var float` scalars updated only on
//        their own confirmed pivot bars (a fixed historical offset via ta.pivotlow/ta.pivothigh, non-
//        repainting); flipLong is read on a LATER, separate bar via ta.crossover, never on the same bar
//        a pivot confirms by construction (a pivot needs pivotRight bars of lookahead to confirm, while
//        flipLong is a same-bar crossover test against whatever pivot values are already latched).
//   OCCUPANCY (LESSONS 24/28/29) - pyramiding=1, flat check gates every entry.
//   CASCADE (HARD LESSON 42/43) - single TP+SL, no partials, LONG at 100% equity (the short-side margin
//        ceiling is not implicated by a long-only build); expect cascadeRatio 1.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale. The SuperTrend line is used
//        ONLY as a one-shot entry trigger, never re-read after entry.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17). CODE BARE -- NO RR FLOOR, NO ADDED FILTER, ONE HALF
// ONLY (credits band 250-500, never-tuned pre-2024 half, per the kill rule):
//   * PRE-2024 HALF (H1) ABOVE 1.0, TRADES ROUGHLY 60-350 -> a genuinely new candidate, provisionally
//     queued for an H2 run in a future cycle (credits permitting) before any filter work.
//   * H1 BELOW 1.0 -> DISCARDED by the kill rule immediately. No filters, no rescue, no H2 run --
//     credits are not spent confirming a dead mechanism.
//   * A MAJORITY WIN RATE WITH ratioAvgWinLoss WELL BELOW 1.0 -> the inverted-payoff shape (HARD LESSON
//     53); report it as that, not as a novel diagnosis.
//   * TRADES WELL BELOW ~30 -> a DIRECTION, not a result (LESSON 12); SuperTrend flips at this factor/
//        length may be too frequent or too rare for a single-symbol single-timeframe test.
//   * A LARGE SHARE OF HOLDS AT maxBars 192 -> the cap is truncating (HARD LESSON 38); report before
//        drawing any conclusion.
//   REPORT GROSS, COMMISSION AND ACHIEVED RATIO alongside net, avg loser and win rate (LESSONS 36/39 and
//     the board's own three-drawdown-category taxonomy).

strategy("BTC Attack89 SuperTrend flip continuation long", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

stFactor   = input.float(3.0, "SuperTrend ATR multiplier")
stAtrLen   = input.int(10, "SuperTrend ATR length")
pivotLeft  = input.int(5, "Pivot confirmation bars, left")
pivotRight = input.int(5, "Pivot confirmation bars, right")
minRpct    = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3)")
maxBars    = input.int(192, "Max bars in trade")

[st, dir] = ta.supertrend(stFactor, stAtrLen)

flipLong = ta.crossover(close, st)

pl = ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)

var float lastPivLow  = na
var float lastPivHigh = na

if not na(pl)
    lastPivLow := pl

if not na(ph)
    lastPivHigh := ph

rLong = not na(lastPivLow) ? close - lastPivLow : na
minR  = close * minRpct / 100
rBig  = not na(rLong) and rLong >= minR

swingAmp = not na(lastPivHigh) and not na(lastPivLow) ? lastPivHigh - lastPivLow : na
swingOk  = not na(swingAmp) and swingAmp > 0

goLong = flipLong and rBig and swingOk

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := lastPivLow
    tpPx   := close + swingAmp
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(st, title="SuperTrend")
plot(lastPivLow, title="LastPivotLow")
plot(lastPivHigh, title="LastPivotHigh")
